From ce66a341624999b0b57296ee4b9afaf5e97dc39d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:05:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/53] Panel settings in Warp's settings; keep the remote_tty
 init line out of shell history

Embedded (remote_tty) builds get a HostAiSettings group (host.ai.* and
host.keys_to_host in settings.toml) with rows in the AI provider settings:
fast model, expanded model, expanded effort, private routing and recent
commands. The host app reads them from Warp's stored settings, so Warp is the
one place to configure the panel. Turning private routing off asks the host to
confirm (window.warpPanelConfirm); recent commands can only be set while it is
on.

The init line remote_tty types into new shells now starts with a space, so
HIST_IGNORE_SPACE keeps it out of the user's history file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
